{"evidence": [{"id": "E1", "activity": "Company-hosted cultural heritage events and celebrations for employees across offices", "quote": "We host cultural events throughout the year to honor the contributions of different groups. For example, we host celebrations for Black History Month, Women’s History Month and Pride Month.", "source_doc": "sustainability_report", "section": "Thriving Organization > Inclusion and Diversity > Creating an Inclusive Workplace", "status": "current", "indicators": "none disclosed", "themes": {"cross_cultural": {"kind": "internal_practice", "criterion": "level 2: specific current internal practice (cultural events) with no reach figures"}}}, {"id": "E2", "activity": "Women@Marvell employee inclusion network offering mentorship, open to all employees", "quote": "Women@Marvell is our inclusion network focused on advancing the careers of women in our company and industry, and membership is open to all Marvell employees.", "source_doc": "sustainability_report", "section": "Thriving Organization > Inclusion and Diversity > Creating an Inclusive Workplace", "status": "current", "indicators": "none disclosed", "themes": {"cross_cultural": {"kind": "internal_practice", "criterion": "level 2: employee network with no membership figures"}}}, {"id": "E3", "activity": "Unconscious bias training delivered to employees worldwide", "quote": "As of FY25, 99% of Marvell employees around the world had completed unconscious bias training.", "source_doc": "sustainability_report", "section": "Thriving Organization > Inclusion and Diversity > Fostering Inclusive Teams", "status": "current", "indicators": "99% of Marvell employees", "themes": {"cross_cultural": {"kind": "internal_practice", "criterion": "level 2: specific current internal inclusion practice"}}}, {"id": "E4", "activity": "Cultural Ambassador program for employees who design regional and global cultural awareness events", "quote": "Lastly, we offer a Cultural Ambassador program for employees who are passionate about inclusion and want to support the design and implementation of regional and global cultural awareness events.", "source_doc": "sustainability_report", "section": "Thriving Organization > Inclusion and Diversity > Fostering Inclusive Teams", "status": "current", "indicators": "none disclosed", "themes": {"cross_cultural": {"kind": "internal_practice", "criterion": "level 2: specific current internal practice with no reach figures"}}}, {"id": "E5", "activity": "Employee participation in the TechWomen mentorship program and hosting of a TechWomen event for emerging women STEM leaders from Africa, the Middle East and Central and South Asia", "quote": "In FY25, we hosted “AI and Beyond: Marvell Welcomes TechWomen 2024,” with over 120 in-person and virtual participants, including our executives and colleagues, TechWomen mentors, emerging STEM leaders from 15 countries and women in tech from across the Bay Area.", "source_doc": "sustainability_report", "section": "Thriving Organization > Inclusion and Diversity > Strengthening Communities and Talent Pipelines Through Partnerships", "status": "current", "indicators": "over 120 in-person and virtual participants; emerging STEM leaders from 15 countries", "themes": {"cross_cultural": {"kind": "connecting_communities", "criterion": "level 2: named cross-cultural mentoring program with limited reach (a single event of about 120 participants)"}}}, {"id": "E6", "activity": "Excellence Scholarships in Vietnam for low-income students and women studying STEM", "quote": "For students in Vietnam who are interested in the sector, we also offer 30 Excellence Scholarships focused on low-income students and women, to fund their education in STEM, in addition to a direct path for potential intern positions.", "source_doc": "sustainability_report", "section": "Thriving Organization > Talent Attraction, Retention, Development and Engagement > Regional Early Career Programs", "status": "current", "indicators": "30 Excellence Scholarships", "themes": {"cross_cultural": {"kind": "connecting_communities", "criterion": "level 2: specific program removing barriers for underrepresented groups, limited in reach"}}}, {"id": "E7", "activity": "Partnerships with the Society of Women Engineers and Society of Hispanic Professional Engineers for learning and development resources", "quote": "Marvell also partners with other organizations, such as the Society of Women Engineers and Society of Hispanic Professional Engineers, to provide learning and development resources.", "source_doc": "sustainability_report", "section": "Thriving Organization > Inclusion and Diversity > Strengthening Communities and Talent Pipelines Through Partnerships", "status": "current", "indicators": "none disclosed", "themes": {"cross_cultural": {"kind": "connecting_communities", "criterion": "level 2: partnerships with organizations serving underrepresented groups, no reach figures"}}}, {"id": "E8", "activity": "Annual global gender pay equity analysis with pay adjustments", "quote": "We perform a global gender pay equity analysis annually, giving us the information we need to minimize unexplained gaps in pay and make adjustments when appropriate.", "source_doc": "sustainability_report", "section": "Thriving Organization > Talent Attraction, Retention, Development and Engagement > Talent Retention", "status": "current", "indicators": "none disclosed", "themes": {"cross_cultural": {"kind": "internal_practice", "criterion": "level 2: specific current inclusive internal practice"}}}],
 "themes": {"cross_cultural": {"score": 2, "coverage": "sufficient", "evidence_ids": ["E1", "E2", "E3", "E4", "E5", "E6", "E7", "E8"], "reason": "Level 2: the 10-K's Inclusion paragraph is general language only, but the sustainability report describes several specific current activities. These are cultural heritage events, the Women@Marvell network, unconscious bias training, a Cultural Ambassador program, pay equity analysis, the TechWomen partnership, Vietnam scholarships for low-income students and women, and SWE/SHPE partnerships. Most have no reach figures. The figures that do appear show limited external reach: one TechWomen event with over 120 participants and 30 scholarships. The 99% training figure is a completion rate, not a measure of reach for a cross-cultural program. There are no network membership figures and no customer access or connecting-communities line of business. Being torn between 2 and 3, I picked the lower level."}},
 "notes": "Score source: 10-K + sustainability report. The 10-K Human Capital > Inclusion section (\"We strive to build a workplace where every individual feels valued...\") is value-statement language only. The 10-K's regional headcount split (49% Americas, 42% APAC, 9% EMEA) describes international operations, which is a trap, and was not counted. The report's U.S. ethnicity and gender demographic tables (hires, turnover, representation by job level) are disclosures only (demographics_only, max 1) and add nothing beyond the activities listed. Girl Scouts STEM badge funding, Rosie's Girls Tech Camp, GSA Women's Leadership Initiative participation and the Tech Exchange computer donation are better treated as Community/STEM education and were not counted separately here. The GSA Executive Accelerator for women started in FY25 but reports no participant figures and was not listed separately. The report's FY25 data cover the prior fiscal year relative to the 10-K's fiscal 2026."}
